# zlib1g CVE-2023-45853 (MiniZip ZIP creation) - will_not_fix in Debian; not used by glean
CVE-2023-45853

# libcap2 CVE-2026-4878 - unfixed in Debian 13; glean runs non-root and does not manage Linux capabilities
CVE-2026-4878

# ncurses CVE-2025-69720 - unfixed in Debian 13; terminal/terminfo tooling is not used by the daemon
CVE-2025-69720

# libsystemd0/libudev1 CVE-2026-29111 - unfixed in Debian 13; systemd/udev APIs are not used by glean
CVE-2026-29111

# perl-base CVEs - all unfixed in Debian 13; glean is a Python daemon and never invokes
# perl, Archive::Tar, or IO-Compress at runtime. Remove entries as Debian ships fixes.
# CVE-2026-42496 Archive::Tar <3.08 symlink extraction; CVE-2026-42497 hardlink extraction;
# CVE-2026-9538 Archive::Tar <3.10 memory exhaustion; CVE-2026-48962 perl-IO-Compress RCE;
# CVE-2026-8376 Perl <=5.43.10 heap buffer overflow;
# CVE-2026-13221 Perl <=5.43.9 silently incorrect results; CVE-2026-57433 Storable <3.41 signed
# integer overflow; CVE-2026-57432 Perl information disclosure via integer overflow.
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-9538
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-57432

# APScheduler CVE-2026-31072 (RCE via insecure deserialization) - no fixed release published
# (4.0.0a6 is the latest). The vulnerable path is persistent data stores deserializing job
# payloads; glean configures no data_store (src/glean/scheduler.py) and uses the default
# in-memory store, so untrusted data never reaches the deserializer. Also ignored in the
# pip-audit step (ci.yml). Remove both ignores when a fixed release ships.
CVE-2026-31072

# util-linux CVE-2026-53615 (integer overflow/wraparound) - unfixed in Debian 13; affects the
# util-linux family (bsdutils, login, mount, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, util-linux). glean is a Python daemon, runs non-root, and never invokes these
# mount/login utilities at runtime. Remove when Debian ships a fix.
CVE-2026-53615

# gzip CVE-2026-41992 (global buffer overflow) - unfixed in Debian 13; glean never shells out to
# the gzip binary (Python compresses via the stdlib). Remove when Debian ships a fix.
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 CVE-2026-54369 (symlink traversal privilege escalation via libacl) - unfixed in
# Debian 13; glean runs non-root and does not manipulate POSIX ACLs. Remove when Debian ships a fix.
CVE-2026-54369
